# CMMC L1 / NIST 800-171 3.13.5 - VNet segmentation primitives
# Platform: Azure
# Check type: az_virtual_network, boolean rollups for subnet + NSG attachment

META
    esp_id `cmmc-l1-3-13-5-az-vnet-segmentation-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `azure`
    criticality `high`

    category `asset_list`
    target_asset_type `Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks`

    title `CMMC L1 SC.L1-3.13.5: Azure VNet uses subnet segmentation with NSG attachment`
    description `Validates that the Azure Virtual Network has subnets defined and that every subnet has an NSG attached. The subnet primitive is the Azure analog of network segmentation for publicly accessible components; the NSG-per-subnet rule ensures every isolation boundary is enforced rather than implicit.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `azure,cmmc-l1,nist-800-171,3-13-5,sc,vnet,subnet-segmentation`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-171:3.13.5`
    control_objective `3.13.5`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `cloud-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Azure:subscription:network-baseline`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `7`
    recommendation `Ensure every subnet in the VNet has an NSG attached. Maintain at least one subnet per trust tier; do not consolidate workloads of different sensitivity into a single subnet.`

    component_id `comp-azure-network`

    impl_3_13_5 `Publicly accessible components are logically separated from internal components by Azure VNet subnets. The VNet is partitioned into subnets representing trust tiers; each subnet has a Network Security Group attached, ensuring traffic at every isolation boundary is subject to explicit allow-list rules rather than open by default. This satisfies the practice intent of subnetworks for publicly accessible components by making the boundary mechanism present and enforced at the network layer.`

META_END

DEF
    # Replace the OBJECT below with one entry per VNet you want this
    # policy to evaluate. Substitute your VNet name and resource group.
    SET vnets union
        OBJECT example_vnet
            name `vnet-example`
            resource_group `rg-example`
        OBJECT_END
    SET_END

    STATE st_vnet_segmented
        found boolean = true
        provisioning_state string = `Succeeded`
        has_subnets boolean = true
        all_subnets_have_nsg boolean = true
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN az_virtual_network
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF st_vnet_segmented
            SET_REF vnets
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
